'''Tainted characters''' are different versions of already existing [[characters]], both in terms of gameplay and design. They are considered completely new characters, raising the total number of characters to 34 in ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Repentance]]''.

They are unlocked by using the {{i|Red Key}}, {{p|Cracked Key}}, or {{P|1=Soul of Cain}} on the left side of the wall in the hall before Mom's Bedroom in {{s|Home}} with each non-Tainted Character.

They can be accessed via the Character select menu by pressing E on the keyboard or RB on controller. The menu will appear a lot more worn with tears in the wallpaper.

As the Tainted Characters, certain unlocks require multiple completion marks: {{E|Satan}}, {{E|Isaac}}, {{E|The Lamb}}, and {{E|???}} all contribute to just one unlock with {{R|Boss Rush}} and {{E|Hush}} accounting for one unlock as well. On top of this, Tainted Characters lack an unlock for defeating {{E|Mom's Heart}} / {{E|It Lives!}} on Hard Mode, {{E|Ultra Greed}}, completing all [[Hard mode]] completion marks, and naturally lack a corresponding Tainted Character unlock. This results in each only having 7 unlocks rather than the standard 15.

